::error file=negative/.env,title=EG001 missing-variable::B is declared in negative/.env.example but missing from negative/.env%0A%0AWhy: Anything that reads B in the default environment gets no value, which usually fails only at runtime or silently falls back to a default.%0A%0AFix: Add `B=` to negative/.env (it is declared in negative/.env.example:1) and set its value. If it is not needed there, mark it optional in the template (`B= # optional`) or put `# envguard-ignore EG001` on the line above it in negative/.env.example.
::warning file=negative/.env,line=1,col=1,title=EG002 undocumented-variable::A is set in negative/.env but not documented in any template%0A%0AWhy: Teammates, CI and deploy targets learn which variables exist from the templates; without an entry, A will be missing wherever this file is not copied.%0A%0AFix: Add `A=` (with an empty or placeholder value, never the real one) to negative/.env.example, or remove it from negative/.env if nothing uses it.
::error file=positive/.env,title=EG001 missing-variable::TEMPLATE_VAR is declared in positive/.env.example but missing from positive/.env%0A%0AWhy: Anything that reads TEMPLATE_VAR in the default environment gets no value, which usually fails only at runtime or silently falls back to a default.%0A%0AFix: Add `TEMPLATE_VAR=` to positive/.env (it is declared in positive/.env.example:1) and set its value. If it is not needed there, mark it optional in the template (`TEMPLATE_VAR= # optional`) or put `# envguard-ignore EG001` on the line above it in positive/.env.example.
::warning file=positive/.env,line=1,col=1,title=EG002 undocumented-variable::DEFINED_VAR is set in positive/.env but not documented in any template%0A%0AWhy: Teammates, CI and deploy targets learn which variables exist from the templates; without an entry, DEFINED_VAR will be missing wherever this file is not copied.%0A%0AFix: Add `DEFINED_VAR=` (with an empty or placeholder value, never the real one) to positive/.env.example, or remove it from positive/.env if nothing uses it.
::warning file=positive/deploy/compose.prod.yaml,line=3,col=19,title=EG011 compose-undefined-variable::positive/deploy/compose.prod.yaml interpolates ${PROD_ONLY}, but there is no positive/deploy/.env next to it and it is not declared in positive/.env.example%0A%0AWhy: Compose substitutes an empty string for an unset PROD_ONLY and only prints a warning, so the container starts with a broken value.%0A%0AFix: Create positive/deploy/.env with `PROD_ONLY=<value>` (Compose reads it automatically), declare `PROD_ONLY=` in a template so others know to set it, or give it a default: `${PROD_ONLY:-value}`.
::warning file=positive/docker-compose.yml,line=5,col=39,title=EG011 compose-undefined-variable::positive/docker-compose.yml interpolates ${DB_PASSWORD}, which is not defined in positive/.env (the file Compose reads) or any template%0A%0AWhy: Compose substitutes an empty string for an unset DB_PASSWORD and only prints a warning, so the container starts with a broken value.%0A%0AFix: Add `DB_PASSWORD=` with a value to positive/.env and document it in a template, or give it a default in the Compose file: `${DB_PASSWORD:-value}`.
::warning file=positive/docker-compose.yml,line=9,col=16,title=EG011 compose-undefined-variable::positive/docker-compose.yml interpolates ${REQUIRED_TOKEN}, which is not defined in positive/.env (the file Compose reads) or any template%0A%0AWhy: The reference uses ${REQUIRED_TOKEN:?...}, so `docker compose up` aborts when it is unset.%0A%0AFix: Add `REQUIRED_TOKEN=` with a value to positive/.env and document it in a template, or give it a default in the Compose file: `${REQUIRED_TOKEN:-value}`.
::warning file=positive/docker-compose.yml,line=12,col=9,title=EG011 compose-undefined-variable::service api: env_file positive/missing.env does not exist%0A%0AWhy: `docker compose up` fails for this service when a required env_file is missing.%0A%0AFix: Create positive/missing.env (for example by copying its template), or make it optional with the long syntax:%0A%0A    env_file:%0A      - path: ./missing.env%0A        required: false
